  "releaseNotes": "See PCN017 for more information about all of the described changes below.\n\n      New:\n      - Targets the Triamec device programming runtime version 6 released together with register layout 20.\n      - Static fields and static auto-properties propagate to customer specific registers.\n      - New programming model to control the execution of Tama programs, their tasks and their state.\n      - Thread.Yield and Thread.Sleep.\n      - Alias tables, axes and other register structures for single source choices.\n      - Embeds source artifacts in the .tama file (configurable).\n      - Supports targeting .NET 10.0 and later.\n\n      Changed:\n      - Tasks are no longer executed in a cyclic manner, allowing for programming sequences. Cyclic behavior now needs to be implemented explicitly by the user.\n\n      Deprecated:\n      - We recommend to stop using application variables and parameters in favor of static fields and static auto-properties.\n\n      Removed:\n      - Support for runtime version 5.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
